# Adapter weights assembled for the Hub. Roughly 100 MB per run and nine runs
# are planned, so they are distributed through the Hub rather than through git.
# The manifest and model card that describe each one live in hasil/ and are
# tracked, so a missing folder here costs provenance nothing.
rilis/

# Everything else under hasil/ IS tracked on purpose: the manifests and the
# prediction files are the evidence behind every number in the thesis, they
# are small, and an examiner has to be able to rescore them without a GPU.
hasil/*.safetensors
hasil/*.bin

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
logs/
hasil/*.jsonl

# Same rule as hasil/, applied to the second Modal account's results.
hasil-akun2/*.jsonl

# Modal API tokens. The file itself lives one level above this repo, but the
# rule is set here so a stray copy inside it can never be committed either.
.env
.env.*

# The report writer and the report it writes. Neither is part of the research:
# naskah/ holds the thesis text, the supervisor's name, and their NIDN and NIPM.
penyusun/
naskah/

# Notes written for the thesis, not documentation of the program.
docs/RENCANA-SKRIPSI.md
docs/aturan-penulisan-skripsi.md
docs/periksa-metopen.md
docs/pustaka-catatan.md
docs/pustaka.bib
docs/lirik-perlu-dicek.md

# Screenshots of the Modal accounts' usage and billing pages.
docs/bukti/

# Everything derived from the source songbook. It is published through Hugging
# Face and Kaggle under its own licence, which is the whole reason the data and
# the code are released separately; committing it here would undo that.
data/
data-v14/
arsip/
rilis-dataset/
rilis-kaggle/

# Adapter weights, same reason as rilis/ above.
rilis-model/
